  "notes": [
    "Valued at what the attackers realised (rule 12), the other tokens at DefiLlama prices (loss.mjs; the anchor attacker's sales of them fetched 84-98% of that): BTCLE at its $582 DefiLlama price is unabsorbable; the attacker bought 769.6 BTCLE for 400,000 USDT as working capital (0xca39c006) and sold 194,987 for 969,105 USDT (0x8a3feead), netting 569,105 USDT. CASHCAT sold in-transaction for 34.71 WETH; RKST for 16.76 ETH (0xb5ea5d1a); IMO in c0ffeebabe's transaction for 15.76 WETH (DefiLlama $89.7k); EDGEN for 8.57 ETH (0x60becfc7; DefiLlama $52.7k).",
    "X (150M of a 1B supply, pair holding about 19 WETH): 46M sold in the exploit transaction for 9.49 WETH and 20M later for 2.52 WETH (0xdb0f2da5); the other 82.1M went back to the vesting's depositor 0x81edadbe (0x686c704e) and realised nothing.",
    "BTCLE excludes the 201 BTCLE the BSC attacker deposited (1 in 0xf2c567f9, a 200 donation in 0x615bc845). The BSC attacker split the exploit into 16 helper-vesting transactions and the payout release 0xbd1b49a2; all are listed.",
    "Earlier VestingCancelled transactions on all four chains are direct cancel() calls by vesting creators, not exploits; the Base, BSC and Robinhood VestingManagers are sibling deployments exploited after the Ethereum anchor."
